# Initial Setup's Frame Type page, ported from GCSViews/ConfigurationView/ConfigFrameClassType.cs.
#
# The claim: the page shows the vehicle's frame - the class button down and the type radio button
# checked are FRAME_CLASS and FRAME_TYPE (Activate, ConfigFrameClassType.cs:36-54) - enables the
# types ArduPilot.Common.ValidList gives that class, and a click on a type writes FRAME_CLASS and
# then FRAME_TYPE at once, with no confirmation (SetFrameParam, ConfigFrameClassType.cs:281-293).
# The vehicle's own echo, params.value.*, is the proof, not the page. The type is put back at the
# end.
#
# Only the type is changed. The class is left alone: FRAME_CLASS decides which motor library the
# copter builds at boot, so changing it on SITL is a reboot-level change and not something this
# test can undo by writing the old value back. The page would write it - a class button writes
# FRAME_CLASS with the current type - so no class button is clicked here.
#
# Needs SITL copter on tcp:127.0.0.1:5760 started from tools/sitl/params/copter.parm, which sets
# FRAME_CLASS 1 (Quad) and FRAME_TYPE 0 (Plus). Run as
#
#   tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/config-frametype.gui -- tcp:127.0.0.1:5760
#
# A run that stops half way leaves FRAME_TYPE at 1 (X); the next run's first expectations fail,
# its restore step still writes 0, and the run after that passes.

screen params
window 1600x1200
# A config.xml of its own, so the "Show me again?" boxes this script clicks are not already
# suppressed by the settings of the machine running it.
env MP_CONFIG_XML $WORK/config.xml
settle 6
# RawParamWarning, on the Full Parameter List's Activate (ConfigRawParams.cs:92): "Show me
# again?" unticked, so no later visit asks, and OK.
click raw-param-warning-again
click raw-param-warning-ok

# Initial Setup lists the page once the vehicle has FRAME_CLASS (InitialSetup.cs:189-191), and
# here parameters are downloaded when asked for.
expect config.frame.available false
click param-download
settle 12
expect params.held > 1000
expect params.value.FRAME_CLASS 1
expect params.value.FRAME_TYPE 0
expect config.frame.available true

click tab-setup
settle 1
expect config.frame.active false
# Frame Type is the second Mandatory Hardware entry of InitialSetup's list (InitialSetup.cs:189).
click setup-page-ConfigMandatory
click setup-page-ConfigFrameClassType
settle 2
expect config.frame.active true
expect config.frame.enabled true

# What Activate read, and what the page shows: the eight class buttons, Quad down, Plus checked.
expect config.frame.classes Undefined,Quad,Hexa,Octa,OctaQuad,Y6,Heli,Tri
expect config.frame.class 1
expect config.frame.class.button Quad
expect config.frame.type 0
expect config.frame.type.radio Plus
# A quad takes Plus, X, V, H, V Tail and A-Tail (Common.cs:19-30); A-Tail has no radio button and
# Y6B is not a quad's, so these five are enabled, and Plus's picture alone is at full opacity.
expect config.frame.types.enabled true
expect config.frame.types 0,1,2,3,4
expect config.frame.bright 0
# Activate's DoClass and DoType each wrote the vehicle's own values back; setParam's "not
# modified as same" means none of them went out (MAVLinkInterface.cs:1647-1651).
expect config.frame.pending 0
expect config.frame.write FRAME_TYPE 0 unchanged
expect config.frame.message none

# X: FRAME_CLASS 1 (unchanged, not sent) then FRAME_TYPE 1, and the vehicle holds it.
click frame-type-1
settle 3
expect config.frame.type 1
expect config.frame.type.radio X
expect config.frame.bright 1
expect config.frame.pending 0
expect config.frame.write FRAME_TYPE 1 accepted
expect config.frame.message none
expect params.value.FRAME_TYPE 1
expect params.value.FRAME_CLASS 1

# And back to Plus.
click frame-type-0
settle 3
expect config.frame.type 0
expect config.frame.type.radio Plus
expect config.frame.write FRAME_TYPE 0 accepted
expect params.value.FRAME_TYPE 0
expect params.value.FRAME_CLASS 1

# Choosing another page deactivates this one, as BackstageView does on every change.
click setup-page-ConfigMandatory
settle 1
expect config.frame.active false
